  "details": "For the time being this feature would be PC only. \n\nThe main idea is this: you would have a speech to text AI that would recognize and transcribe languages into text locally on the users machine, then the text is sent to a cloud server to be translated into English (maybe done locally?) and then an AI text to speech, based on the users own voice would speak the text in English (also generated on the users machine). \n\nThis is effectively an AI powered translator. The great thing about it is that it wouldn't impact server cost that much as most of the processing would be client end. \n\nThe benefits are twofold, one is greater accessibility and  potential growth of the user base due to ease of communicating (which is important for a social game) and the other is helping to learn English (as you hear English being pronounced in your own voice).",
